<ResourceDictionary xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml/presentation"
                    xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
                    xmlns:utu="using:Uno.Toolkit.UI">

  <!--
    NeuHighContrast. Merge this after NeuTheme and every Neu control loses its
    depth and gains a 1px NeuInk outline instead:

      <ResourceDictionary.MergedDictionaries>
        <neu:NeuTheme />
        <ResourceDictionary Source="ms-appx:///Neu.Uno/Theme/Neu.HighContrast.xaml" />
      </ResourceDictionary.MergedDictionaries>

    It restates the six depth collections and nothing else. Because templates
    reference depth only by name (CLAUDE.md rule 2), restating the names is
    enough to reach every control at once - no template in the library knows
    this file exists, and a consumer's own Neu-anatomy control is covered too.

    Every depth step becomes the same outline, NeuFlat included. That is
    deliberate: a pressed or checked control must not lose its silhouette, and
    it stays legible because rule 5 already requires a second channel - a glyph,
    an ink change, an amber bar - for every state. Depth was never carrying a
    state on its own.

    The outline is an INNER shadow, which is not a stylistic choice. An outward
    ring needs a pixel of layout slack on every side and silently loses the
    edges that do not have it: drawn outward, an Expander body sized exactly to
    its content rendered with its left and right edges and no top or bottom.
    An inner ring is inside the surface's own bounds, so nothing can clip it.

    Collapsing NeuFlat to the outline is the first of three deviations from
    the Interaction Brief. The other two, all of them recorded in
    docs/decisions.md as D11:

    1. The outline lands on every Neu surface, not only on interactives. The
       collections are shared, so a dictionary swap cannot tell a Button from a
       NeuSurface. With depth gone, an unoutlined surface has no edge at all.
    2. The focus and error rings widen from spread 2 to 3 rather than staying
       put. At the same width they would differ from the resting outline by hue
       alone, which is the one channel high contrast is least able to spend.

    Colors are untouched: the palette already clears the contrast floors in
    CLAUDE.md rule 12 in both themes, enforced by tools/contrast-check.ps1.
  -->

  <ResourceDictionary.ThemeDictionaries>

    <ResourceDictionary x:Key="Light">
      <!-- Every depth step is the same outline: there is no depth left to read. -->
      <utu:ShadowCollection x:Key="NeuRaisedSm">
        <utu:Shadow IsInner="True"
                    OffsetX="0"
                    OffsetY="0"
                    BlurRadius="{StaticResource NeuHighContrastBlur}"
                    Spread="{StaticResource NeuHighContrastOutlineSpread}"
                    Color="{StaticResource NeuInk}"
                    Opacity="1" />
      </utu:ShadowCollection>

      <utu:ShadowCollection x:Key="NeuRaisedMd">
        <utu:Shadow IsInner="True"
                    OffsetX="0"
                    OffsetY="0"
                    BlurRadius="{StaticResource NeuHighContrastBlur}"
                    Spread="{StaticResource NeuHighContrastOutlineSpread}"
                    Color="{StaticResource NeuInk}"
                    Opacity="1" />
      </utu:ShadowCollection>

      <utu:ShadowCollection x:Key="NeuRaisedLg">
        <utu:Shadow IsInner="True"
                    OffsetX="0"
                    OffsetY="0"
                    BlurRadius="{StaticResource NeuHighContrastBlur}"
                    Spread="{StaticResource NeuHighContrastOutlineSpread}"
                    Color="{StaticResource NeuInk}"
                    Opacity="1" />
      </utu:ShadowCollection>

      <utu:ShadowCollection x:Key="NeuInsetSm">
        <utu:Shadow IsInner="True"
                    OffsetX="0"
                    OffsetY="0"
                    BlurRadius="{StaticResource NeuHighContrastBlur}"
                    Spread="{StaticResource NeuHighContrastOutlineSpread}"
                    Color="{StaticResource NeuInk}"
                    Opacity="1" />
      </utu:ShadowCollection>

      <utu:ShadowCollection x:Key="NeuInsetMd">
        <utu:Shadow IsInner="True"
                    OffsetX="0"
                    OffsetY="0"
                    BlurRadius="{StaticResource NeuHighContrastBlur}"
                    Spread="{StaticResource NeuHighContrastOutlineSpread}"
                    Color="{StaticResource NeuInk}"
                    Opacity="1" />
      </utu:ShadowCollection>

      <utu:ShadowCollection x:Key="NeuFlat">
        <utu:Shadow IsInner="True"
                    OffsetX="0"
                    OffsetY="0"
                    BlurRadius="{StaticResource NeuHighContrastBlur}"
                    Spread="{StaticResource NeuHighContrastOutlineSpread}"
                    Color="{StaticResource NeuInk}"
                    Opacity="1" />
      </utu:ShadowCollection>

      <!-- Wider than the outline, so focus and error read on width, not hue alone. -->
      <utu:ShadowCollection x:Key="NeuFocusRing">
        <utu:Shadow OffsetX="0"
                    OffsetY="0"
                    BlurRadius="{StaticResource NeuHighContrastBlur}"
                    Spread="{StaticResource NeuHighContrastRingSpread}"
                    Color="{StaticResource NeuAccent}"
                    Opacity="1" />
      </utu:ShadowCollection>

      <utu:ShadowCollection x:Key="NeuAlertRing">
